  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_a2988f7945ef4e72808bd64a323b7af9",
      "statement": "Routing builds one OpenAI function tool per configured collection named `query_<collection.lower()>` via `build_routing_tools`, and `retrieve_documents` maps each returned tool call's name back to a collection name (e.g. `query_lipitor` -> `Lipitor`) using its `query` argument as the search text, so collection names must stay consistent across runtime configuration, ingestion targets, and evals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/graph/nodes/retrieve.py#L110-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:71b079e5a0685c62b86b3d99bfaf10d1c1b1ed0c6c7653db60049089a1b84d4e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/retrieval.py#L13-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33ed8ca13164c1e105e103de3e7db2a3e4563ff9da22bd1a19cef87a87c25af3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b781b620c12a420eb02dbcc2063dbbff",
      "statement": "A routing failure is caught and degraded to an empty tool-call list rather than aborting the request, and each per-collection search is retried up to three times with 1s/2s backoff on the active arm's transient SDK error class (WeaviateBaseError for weaviate/pageindex, PineconeException for pinecone).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/graph/nodes/retrieve.py#L38-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:66d31fd39ac0e6762f7829a25a8dd03abc12d9876a198fd27e5c68ccc87abb4d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/graph/nodes/retrieve.py#L85-L149",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51224eeb84495e7b71ad747f6ff0f39b6465e2090e019555705cfcf613af1be5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fa6a4be87a22411b889229ddf0035cf7",
      "statement": "`hybrid_search` calls Weaviate's `collection.query.hybrid` with `query_properties=[\"contextualized\"]`, a default `limit=4`, `alpha=0.65`, `fusion_type=HybridFusion.RELATIVE_SCORE`, and `return_metadata=MetadataQuery(score=True)`, so the hybrid query targets only the contextualized chunk text, weights semantic signal over keyword signal, and exposes the Weaviate relevance score.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/retrieval.py#L61-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3b9e6e56b1bf256b8e07f3f84654b0fd76ac222d5ee32768b29ec5e1de1ab7b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_193896c77a154ddf933b9af32bec2cf5",
      "statement": "`to_query_documents` sets `QueryDocument.doc_id` to the Weaviate object's UUID string and packs all remaining returned properties except `contextualized` into `QueryDocument.metadata`; that UUID, not the ingested chunk `id_`, is the durable runtime document identity used for citations, while `id_` survives only as metadata used by eval chunk-recall.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/processors/retrieval.py#L38-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:381f82d0dba14e225fc20e95ddd71696630a18ffa21480b6b5df25a22aa26507:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3529ea1c8b949da8bb6142dd7db2f87",
      "statement": "`storage/vector_store.py` creates each Weaviate collection with the `text2vec_openai` vectorizer and exactly five properties: `id_` (INT), `text` (TEXT), `contextualized` (TEXT), `doc_source` (TEXT), and `page_numbers` (INT_ARRAY); any other JSON fields present in an ingest row, including chunk metadata, are discarded on import.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/storage/vector_store.py#L101-L136",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c40775ce5f256e19798d28b0fa988f5accce6120868da246e24115d07420a5e8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/storage/vector_store.py#L41-L50",
